>>
Rule 1 (inputs have equal ranks and identical shapes)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ (ndim(v_1) = 0 ∨ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i))
>>
Rule 2 (no mismatch at non-singleton dimension 0: equal or broadcastable)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) = 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 0) ∨ ((ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0) ∧ (shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 0) ∨ shape(v_1, 0) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, 0) = 1))
>>
Rule 4 (out shape matches inputs when ranks match)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ndim(v_2) = ndim(v_3) ∧ (ndim(v_1) = 0 ∨ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_1, i) ∧ shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i))
>>
Rule 5 (if input is empty along dim 0, other must be compatible at dim 0)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) = 0) then (shape(v_2, 0) = 0 ∨ shape(v_2, 0) = 1)
